VERSION:   4
COMMENT: epsilon-iron (Fe), hcp, P6_3/mmc - Dewaele et al. (2006) Phys. Rev. Lett. 97, 215504, doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.97.215504, table III
COMMENT: Vinet fit at 300 K between 17 and 197 GPa (He medium, ruby or W scale): V0=11.214(49) A3/atom, K0=163.4(7.9) GPa, K0P=5.38(16)
COMMENT: WARNING: the EOS keyword is a pyFAI extension, other programs read K0/K0P as Birch-Murnaghan
COMMENT: Thermal model of the source: expanded Mie-Gruneisen-Debye, theta0=417 K, gamma0=1.875, gamma_inf=1.305, beta=gamma0/(gamma0-gamma_inf), a0=3.7e-5 /K, m=1.87, e0=1.95e-4 /K, g=1.339, reference 300 K, constrained by shock-wave data up to 200 GPa
COMMENT: ALPHAT, DALPHADT, DK0DT, DK0PDT fitted on this model (thermal pressure, as in Dioptas) between 20 and 200 GPa and 300 and 4000 K: pressure within 1.3 GPa (0.1 GPa rms), temperature within 30 K
COMMENT: epsilon-Fe is stable above about 16 GPa: V0 is an extrapolation
COMMENT: c/a=1.603 read on the inset of Fig. 1 at 20 GPa; c/a decreases to 1.597 at 150-200 GPa, not described by the EoS
COMMENT: Intensities calculated (Cu Ka, Cromer-Mann form factor of Cl used for Fe, no thermal factor)
